# Line endings, per docs/engineering/cross-platform-builds.md §9.
#
# MyGo recognises its own generated files by a header that ends in LF
# (internal/nativegen/parse.go, isGenerated). With core.autocrlf=true the
# committed bindings arrive with CRLF, MyGo stops recognising them, and
# `mygo native check` regenerates a different interface hash: bb7eb37b2f2b16dd
# instead of 006d88f0942bea95. Keep generated sources and their inputs LF on
# every platform; REL-05 evidence records the reproduction.
#
# PowerShell keeps the Windows default (CRLF): do not add *.ps1 here.
*.go text eol=lf
*.rs text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
